{
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "topic-group:discovery",
      "type": "group",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 420,
      "width": 4400,
      "height": 19033,
      "label": "Discover attack surfaces",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method-group:path-hosts",
      "type": "group",
      "x": 35,
      "y": 3612,
      "width": 4080,
      "height": 1707,
      "label": "Validate the source path and discover hosts",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method-group:tcp-coverage",
      "type": "group",
      "x": 35,
      "y": 5444,
      "width": 4080,
      "height": 1304,
      "label": "Discover TCP ports with SYN or connect scans",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method-group:identify-app",
      "type": "group",
      "x": 35,
      "y": 6873,
      "width": 4080,
      "height": 6643,
      "label": "Identify applications and validate selected NSE checks",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method-group:udp-coverage",
      "type": "group",
      "x": 35,
      "y": 13641,
      "width": 4080,
      "height": 1304,
      "label": "Probe UDP and resolve ambiguous silence",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method-group:result-validation",
      "type": "group",
      "x": 35,
      "y": 15070,
      "width": 4080,
      "height": 1328,
      "label": "Validate uncertain results and rebuild the service queue",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method-group:windows-discovery",
      "type": "group",
      "x": 35,
      "y": 16523,
      "width": 4080,
      "height": 1352,
      "label": "Enumerate reachable endpoints from a Windows source",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method-group:unknown-port",
      "type": "group",
      "x": 35,
      "y": 18000,
      "width": 4080,
      "height": 1328,
      "label": "Discriminate unknown listeners and use scanner alternatives",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "topic:discovery",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 60,
      "y": 440,
      "width": 1800,
      "height": 140,
      "text": "# Discover attack surfaces\n\nStart with an assigned address/list and your actual source interface; no open service is assumed.",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "flow:discovery:home",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 60,
      "y": 620,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 240,
      "text": "## Investigation flow\n\nDiscover attack surfaces\n\n · \n\nBranches describe evidence and missing conditions. Follow one useful lead, then return to unfinished coverage.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "flow:discovery:check-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 560,
      "y": 620,
      "width": 760,
      "height": 324,
      "text": "## Confirm the source route\n\nRun from the machine that will send the scan. Keep the assigned scope explicit.\n\n```bash\nip addr\nip route get TARGET\nnmap -sn SUBNET -oA host-discovery\n```\n\n**Validate the source path and discover hosts — on this canvas**"
    },
    {
      "id": "flow:discovery:check-0-finding-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1610,
      "y": 620,
      "width": 610,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### A route selects the expected interface/source\n\nReachability still needs a probe; a route lookup alone is not a live host.\n\n**Discover TCP ports with SYN or connect scans — on this canvas**",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "flow:discovery:check-0-fallback",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2380,
      "y": 620,
      "width": 610,
      "height": 204,
      "text": "### Unresolved / alternate check\n\nNo response from host discovery: test the assigned host without assuming it is offline.\n\n**Discover TCP ports with SYN or connect scans — on this canvas**",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "flow:discovery:check-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 560,
      "y": 1124,
      "width": 760,
      "height": 324,
      "text": "## Build a TCP port list with Nmap\n\nThe command below scans all TCP ports with SYN privileges. Create the scans output directory first; use the complete connect-scan variant when unprivileged. Keep the fast initial pass distinct from full coverage.\n\n```bash\nsudo nmap -sS -n -p- -oA scans/tcp-all TARGET\n```\n\n**Discover TCP ports with SYN or connect scans — on this canvas**"
    },
    {
      "id": "flow:discovery:check-1-finding-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1610,
      "y": 1124,
      "width": 610,
      "height": 204,
      "text": "### An open TCP port\n\nRun focused service detection on the discovered ports, including nonstandard ones.\n\n**Identify applications and validate selected NSE checks — on this canvas**",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "flow:discovery:check-1-fallback",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2380,
      "y": 1124,
      "width": 610,
      "height": 204,
      "text": "### Unresolved / alternate check\n\nOnly TCP was checked: investigate UDP when the objective or DNS/SNMP/RPC clues call for it.\n\n**Probe UDP and resolve ambiguous silence — on this canvas**",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "flow:discovery:check-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 560,
      "y": 1628,
      "width": 760,
      "height": 300,
      "text": "## Identify the responding application\n\nKeep the endpoint and raw service output; choose the matching client from its response.\n\n```bash\nnmap -Pn -sV -p PORTS TARGET -oA selected-services\nnmap --script-help SCRIPT_NAME\n```\n\n**Identify applications and validate selected NSE checks — on this canvas**"
    },
    {
      "id": "flow:discovery:check-2-finding-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1610,
      "y": 1628,
      "width": 610,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### SMB/RPC responds\n\nCheck anonymous or known-identity share access.\n\n[[tracks/02 Services.canvas|Enumerate SMB/RPC shares, files and identities → 02 Services]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "flow:discovery:check-2-finding-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1610,
      "y": 1853,
      "width": 610,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### An HTTP response or redirect\n\nResolve the correct scheme and hostname before directory discovery.\n\n[[tracks/03 Web.canvas|Establish scheme, host, redirects and request state → 03 Web]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "flow:discovery:check-2-finding-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1610,
      "y": 2078,
      "width": 610,
      "height": 204,
      "text": "### An unrecognized listener\n\nSend a protocol-specific probe instead of choosing an exploit by port number.\n\n**Discriminate unknown listeners and use scanner alternatives — on this canvas**",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "flow:discovery:check-2-fallback",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2380,
      "y": 1628,
      "width": 610,
      "height": 204,
      "text": "### Unresolved / alternate check\n\nResults conflict with client behavior: rebuild the endpoint queue from confirmed responses.\n\n**Validate uncertain results and rebuild the service queue — on this canvas**",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "notes:discovery",
      "type": "file",
      "file": "notes/discovery.md",
      "x": 60,
      "y": 2512,
      "width": 2100,
      "height": 850
    },
    {
      "id": "notes-label:discovery",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2350,
      "y": 2512,
      "width": 1400,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "## Full procedures and alternatives\n\nThe adjacent embedded note is readable here. Scroll inside it for complete variants. Commands and decisions continue below.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:path-hosts:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 70,
      "y": 3787,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Validate the source path and discover hosts\n\nNo response, a new subnet, or uncertainty about the interface and route",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:path-hosts:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 570,
      "y": 3747,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 228,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\nip addr\nip route get TARGET\nnmap -sn SUBNET -oA host-discovery\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:path-hosts:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 3727,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nThe route names the intended interface/source; a responder is evidence from that source, not a global reachability claim.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:path-hosts:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 3973,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nCheck scope, target state and whether host-discovery probes are permitted by this path.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:path-hosts:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 3677,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nThe assigned route is correct and the selected application responds: proceed to service coverage.\n\n**Verify:** Record source address/interface, route and the exact responding endpoint; a missing ping response does not prove a host is down.\n\n[[notes/discovery.md#path-hosts|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:path-hosts:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 4018,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nThe route points outside the assigned VPN: repair that route before evaluating the target.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:path-hosts:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 4239,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nNo discovery response but a plausible route exists: the host may filter probes; test a justified selected port.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:path-hosts:action",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 3677,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Procedure entry — full sequence in the note\n\n```bash\nmkdir -p scans\nip -br addr\nip route get TARGET\n```\n\n[[notes/discovery.md#path-hosts|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:path-hosts:next-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 4043,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Discover TCP ports with SYN or connect scans\n\n**When:** An assigned host needs an initial service queue or full TCP coverage\n\n**Still required:** SYN scanning needs raw-packet privileges; connect scanning needs OS TCP connections; specify selected versus full port coverage\n\n**Discover TCP ports with SYN or connect scans — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:path-hosts:next-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 4374,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Probe UDP and resolve ambiguous silence\n\n**When:** TCP enumeration is incomplete for the objective or DNS/SNMP/RPC clues suggest UDP\n\n**Still required:** Raw-packet access and UDP reachability from the real source; bounded or full selection must be explicit\n\n**Probe UDP and resolve ambiguous silence — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:path-hosts:next-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 4705,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Relay a single TCP service through a fixed forward\n\n**When:** One reachable pivot can connect to one internal TCP destination\n\n**Still required:** A bindable pivot listener, source-to-listener access and pivot-to-destination connectivity\n\n[[tracks/10 Pivoting.canvas|Relay a single TCP service through a fixed forward → 10 Pivoting]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:path-hosts:next-3",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 5012,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Enumerate reachable endpoints from a Windows source\n\n**When:** The useful vantage point is a Windows host without Nmap\n\n**Still required:** A permitted Windows shell, explicit target list and built-in networking support\n\n**Enumerate reachable endpoints from a Windows source — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:tcp-coverage:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 70,
      "y": 5619,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Discover TCP ports with SYN or connect scans\n\nAn assigned host needs an initial service queue or full TCP coverage",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:tcp-coverage:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 570,
      "y": 5579,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 204,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\nnmap -Pn -sT --top-ports 1000 TARGET -oA tcp-initial\nnmap -Pn -sT -p- TARGET -oA tcp-full\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:tcp-coverage:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 5559,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nThe high listener exists outside the first selection; its application label remains provisional.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:tcp-coverage:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 5805,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nConfirm scan completion, source, errors and application behavior on each interesting port.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:tcp-coverage:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 5509,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nA focused connection and application response confirm the listener: queue its service.\n\n**Verify:** Retain the selected port set, source context, completion/errors and raw output; follow open ports with focused application evidence.\n\n[[notes/discovery.md#tcp-coverage|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:tcp-coverage:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 5850,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nThe earlier result cannot be reproduced after a completed focused check: retire that stale listener hypothesis.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:tcp-coverage:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 6071,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nFiltered ports or interrupted scans leave coverage/reachability unresolved; save the limit and choose a focused check.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:tcp-coverage:action",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 5509,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 228,
      "text": "### Procedure entry — full sequence in the note\n\n```bash\nsudo nmap -sS -n -oA scans/tcp-initial TARGET\n```\n\n[[notes/discovery.md#tcp-coverage|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:tcp-coverage:next-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 5827,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Identify applications and validate selected NSE checks\n\n**When:** A listener has a port-based label or uncertain version\n\n**Still required:** A reachable selected port; scripts must match the application and permitted assessment behavior\n\n**Identify applications and validate selected NSE checks — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:tcp-coverage:next-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 6134,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Enumerate SMB/RPC shares, files and identities\n\n**When:** SMB/RPC endpoints, domain clues or new credentials\n\n**Still required:** Reachable SMB/RPC; anonymous, guest, local or domain context must be explicit; share and filesystem ACLs both matter\n\n[[tracks/02 Services.canvas|Enumerate SMB/RPC shares, files and identities → 02 Services]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:tcp-coverage:next-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 6441,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Establish scheme, host, redirects and request state\n\n**When:** An HTTP endpoint, redirect or hostname-dependent response\n\n**Still required:** Correct scheme/port and virtual host; saved cookies/headers for authenticated comparisons\n\n[[tracks/03 Web.canvas|Establish scheme, host, redirects and request state → 03 Web]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:identify-app:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 70,
      "y": 7048,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Identify applications and validate selected NSE checks\n\nA listener has a port-based label or uncertain version",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:identify-app:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 570,
      "y": 7008,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\nnmap -Pn -sV -p PORTS TARGET -oA selected-services\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:identify-app:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 6988,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nAn HTTP response on a nonstandard port routes investigation to application mapping; a product string is still only fingerprint evidence.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:identify-app:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 7234,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nVerify normal requests, hostname/TLS requirements and exact build/configuration before selecting an exploit.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:identify-app:checks",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 570,
      "y": 7248,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Validate the condition\n\n```bash\nnmap -Pn -sV -p PORTS TARGET -oA selected-services\nnmap --script-help SCRIPT_NAME\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:identify-app:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 6938,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nNative protocol responses agree with the fingerprint: use that service's enumeration guide.\n\n**Verify:** Preserve the responding product/version evidence and distinguish an inferred fingerprint from a confirmed vulnerable build.\n\n[[notes/discovery.md#identify-app|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:identify-app:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 7279,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nA presumed SSH port instead speaks HTTP: discard the SSH-specific method for that endpoint.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:identify-app:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 7500,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nGeneric banners or timeouts do not identify a build; try protocol-aware/TLS discrimination.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:identify-app:action",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 6938,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 228,
      "text": "### Procedure entry — full sequence in the note\n\n```bash\nnmap -sT -n -sV -p PORTS -oA scans/tcp-services TARGET\n```\n\n[[notes/discovery.md#identify-app|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:identify-app:next-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 7256,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Discriminate unknown listeners and use scanner alternatives\n\n**When:** A nonstandard listener, slow TCP discovery or a scanner-specific candidate\n\n**Still required:** Explicit bounded scope; raw scanning alternatives need their required privileges and conservative rates\n\n**Discriminate unknown listeners and use scanner alternatives — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:identify-app:next-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 7587,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Establish scheme, host, redirects and request state\n\n**When:** An HTTP endpoint, redirect or hostname-dependent response\n\n**Still required:** Correct scheme/port and virtual host; saved cookies/headers for authenticated comparisons\n\n[[tracks/03 Web.canvas|Establish scheme, host, redirects and request state → 03 Web]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:identify-app:next-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 7894,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Match a public exploit to the actual component and configuration\n\n**When:** A product/version clue, advisory or component-specific public PoC\n\n**Still required:** Exact vulnerable build/configuration, required access and endpoint behavior; reviewable source and a verifiable expected effect\n\n[[tracks/04 Public Exploits.canvas|Match a public exploit to the actual component and configuration → 04 Public Exploits]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:identify-app:next-3",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 8201,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Inspect rsync modules and retrieve selected artifacts\n\n**When:** An rsync daemon banner, TCP/873 listener or disclosed rsync module\n\n**Still required:** Reachable rsync daemon and a module/path readable by the anonymous or supplied account\n\n[[tracks/02 Services.canvas|Inspect rsync modules and retrieve selected artifacts → 02 Services]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:identify-app:next-4",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 8508,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Retrieve an evidence-backed file over TFTP\n\n**When:** A UDP/69 service plus a plausible filename from configuration, source or boot metadata\n\n**Still required:** Reachable TFTP service and an exact server-relative filename permitted for read or write\n\n[[tracks/02 Services.canvas|Retrieve an evidence-backed file over TFTP → 02 Services]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:identify-app:next-5",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 8839,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Use anonymous or authenticated FTP file access\n\n**When:** An FTP banner or accessible listing\n\n**Still required:** Anonymous login allowed or a valid FTP identity; data-channel connectivity and object-specific read/write rights\n\n[[tracks/02 Services.canvas|Use anonymous or authenticated FTP file access → 02 Services]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:identify-app:next-6",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 9146,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Use SSH passwords, keys and forwarding-capable access\n\n**When:** An SSH service and a known password, private key or agent context\n\n**Still required:** Compatible authentication method, correct user, accepted key policy and the requested shell/subsystem permission\n\n[[tracks/02 Services.canvas|Use SSH passwords, keys and forwarding-capable access → 02 Services]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:identify-app:next-7",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 9453,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Enumerate SMTP identities and accessible mailbox protocols\n\n**When:** SMTP capabilities or mail-related account clues\n\n**Still required:** Reachable SMTP/POP3/IMAP service; enumeration or mailbox access must be enabled for the selected context\n\n[[tracks/02 Services.canvas|Enumerate SMTP identities and accessible mailbox protocols → 02 Services]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:identify-app:next-8",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 9760,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Expand names through DNS records and zone transfers\n\n**When:** A DNS server, domain name or host aliases\n\n**Still required:** Reachable DNS transport and relevant authoritative zone; AXFR requires an allowed TCP zone transfer\n\n[[tracks/02 Services.canvas|Expand names through DNS records and zone transfers → 02 Services]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:identify-app:next-9",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 10067,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Inspect RPC/NFS exports and effective file identity\n\n**When:** RPC/NFS listeners or export information\n\n**Still required:** Reachable RPC/NFS transports, permitted client address and an export whose UID/GID mapping grants relevant access\n\n[[tracks/02 Services.canvas|Inspect RPC/NFS exports and effective file identity → 02 Services]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:identify-app:next-10",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 10374,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Enumerate SMB/RPC shares, files and identities\n\n**When:** SMB/RPC endpoints, domain clues or new credentials\n\n**Still required:** Reachable SMB/RPC; anonymous, guest, local or domain context must be explicit; share and filesystem ACLs both matter\n\n[[tracks/02 Services.canvas|Enumerate SMB/RPC shares, files and identities → 02 Services]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:identify-app:next-11",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 10681,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Extract configuration and process information through SNMP\n\n**When:** UDP/161 evidence or an exposed management plane\n\n**Still required:** An accepted read community or SNMPv3 identity/security level; transport and view permissions\n\n[[tracks/02 Services.canvas|Extract configuration and process information through SNMP → 02 Services]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:identify-app:next-12",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 10988,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Use MySQL/MariaDB data and file primitives\n\n**When:** A MySQL-compatible service and valid application/database credentials\n\n**Still required:** Database authentication and exact schema/file privileges; secure_file_priv and server filesystem identity constrain file actions\n\n[[tracks/02 Services.canvas|Use MySQL/MariaDB data and file primitives → 02 Services]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:identify-app:next-13",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 11319,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Use SQL Server rights, impersonation and command facilities\n\n**When:** SQL Server credentials or a Windows identity accepted by the database\n\n**Still required:** Correct SQL versus Windows authentication; database role and configuration must permit the requested operation\n\n[[tracks/02 Services.canvas|Use SQL Server rights, impersonation and command facilities → 02 Services]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:identify-app:next-14",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 11650,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Use PostgreSQL data and privileged program execution\n\n**When:** PostgreSQL access or an application connection string\n\n**Still required:** Accepted connection/database role; COPY PROGRAM needs the corresponding server privilege and an executable OS context\n\n[[tracks/02 Services.canvas|Use PostgreSQL data and privileged program execution → 02 Services]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:identify-app:next-15",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 11957,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Inspect Redis access and persistence boundaries\n\n**When:** A Redis listener or application cache credentials\n\n**Still required:** Reachability and accepted authentication/ACL commands; persistence writes need CONFIG rights, destination permissions and a consumer\n\n[[tracks/02 Services.canvas|Inspect Redis access and persistence boundaries → 02 Services]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:identify-app:next-16",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 12264,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Triage Oracle listener and database identity\n\n**When:** An Oracle TNS listener or connection descriptor\n\n**Still required:** Correct service/SID, reachable database transport and valid database credentials for authenticated work\n\n[[tracks/02 Services.canvas|Triage Oracle listener and database identity → 02 Services]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:identify-app:next-17",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 12571,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Validate RDP, WinRM, VNC and Telnet access contexts\n\n**When:** An exposed remote-access application and compatible known credentials\n\n**Still required:** Enabled destination service, matching authentication and protocol-specific logon/session rights\n\n[[tracks/02 Services.canvas|Validate RDP, WinRM, VNC and Telnet access contexts → 02 Services]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:identify-app:next-18",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 12902,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Discover LDAP naming contexts and authenticated search\n\n**When:** LDAP/Kerberos listeners or a probable AD domain\n\n**Still required:** Reachable directory; anonymous query permission or valid bind identity; required signing/TLS and naming context\n\n[[tracks/02 Services.canvas|Discover LDAP naming contexts and authenticated search → 02 Services]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:identify-app:next-19",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 13209,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Investigate SIP/IRC identity and configuration clues\n\n**When:** A confirmed SIP or IRC application\n\n**Still required:** Application-specific request format; permitted registration/channel/configuration access\n\n[[tracks/02 Services.canvas|Investigate SIP/IRC identity and configuration clues → 02 Services]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:udp-coverage:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 70,
      "y": 13816,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Probe UDP and resolve ambiguous silence\n\nTCP enumeration is incomplete for the objective or DNS/SNMP/RPC clues suggest UDP",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:udp-coverage:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 570,
      "y": 13776,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\nsudo nmap -Pn -sU --top-ports 20 --reason TARGET -oA udp-initial\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:udp-coverage:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 13756,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nA DNS response confirms a UDP application; open|filtered SNMP silence is a candidate requiring a correctly formatted request.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:udp-coverage:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 14002,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nCheck accepted service parameters, response identity and possible ICMP rate limiting.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:udp-coverage:checks",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 570,
      "y": 14016,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Validate the condition\n\n```bash\nsudo nmap -Pn -sU --top-ports 20 --reason TARGET -oA udp-initial\nsudo nmap -Pn -sU -sV -p 53,161 TARGET -oA udp-focused\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:udp-coverage:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 13706,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nA service-native request returns the expected OID/record: enumerate that application.\n\n**Verify:** Use an application response for a confirmed service; document unresolved silence, coverage and ICMP rate-limit effects.\n\n[[notes/discovery.md#udp-coverage|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:udp-coverage:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 14047,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nAn explicit port-unreachable response rules out that UDP endpoint for this source/time.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:udp-coverage:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 14268,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nSilence can mean open or filtered; use a justified application-aware probe rather than declaring either.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:udp-coverage:action",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 13706,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 228,
      "text": "### Procedure entry — full sequence in the note\n\n```bash\nsudo nmap -sU -n --top-ports 20 -oA scans/udp-top20 TARGET\n```\n\n[[notes/discovery.md#udp-coverage|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:udp-coverage:next-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 14024,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Extract configuration and process information through SNMP\n\n**When:** UDP/161 evidence or an exposed management plane\n\n**Still required:** An accepted read community or SNMPv3 identity/security level; transport and view permissions\n\n[[tracks/02 Services.canvas|Extract configuration and process information through SNMP → 02 Services]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:udp-coverage:next-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 14331,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Expand names through DNS records and zone transfers\n\n**When:** A DNS server, domain name or host aliases\n\n**Still required:** Reachable DNS transport and relevant authoritative zone; AXFR requires an allowed TCP zone transfer\n\n[[tracks/02 Services.canvas|Expand names through DNS records and zone transfers → 02 Services]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:udp-coverage:next-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 14638,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Inspect RPC/NFS exports and effective file identity\n\n**When:** RPC/NFS listeners or export information\n\n**Still required:** Reachable RPC/NFS transports, permitted client address and an export whose UID/GID mapping grants relevant access\n\n[[tracks/02 Services.canvas|Inspect RPC/NFS exports and effective file identity → 02 Services]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:result-validation:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 70,
      "y": 15245,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Validate uncertain results and rebuild the service queue\n\nScanners disagree, a result is ambiguous, or a new identity changes accessible behavior",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:result-validation:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 570,
      "y": 15205,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 204,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\nnc -nvz TARGET PORT\nnmap -Pn -sT -p PORT --reason TARGET\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:result-validation:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 15185,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nIndependent TCP reachability supports an endpoint candidate, not credentials, read permission or execution.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:result-validation:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 15431,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 132,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nIdentify the application and validate the particular next-layer action.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:result-validation:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 15135,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nThe protocol answers and the intended access check succeeds: record that specific capability.\n\n**Verify:** Record which layer was demonstrated: transport, application, authentication, read/write or execution.\n\n[[notes/discovery.md#result-validation|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:result-validation:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 15476,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nThe expected protocol is absent despite a listener: reject that protocol-specific hypothesis.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:result-validation:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 15697,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nConflicting source/time results need a controlled repeat and route comparison.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:result-validation:action",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 15135,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 228,
      "text": "### Procedure entry — full sequence in the note\n\n```bash\nnc -nv -w 3 -z TARGET PORTS\n```\n\n[[notes/discovery.md#result-validation|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:result-validation:next-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 15453,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Identify applications and validate selected NSE checks\n\n**When:** A listener has a port-based label or uncertain version\n\n**Still required:** A reachable selected port; scripts must match the application and permitted assessment behavior\n\n**Identify applications and validate selected NSE checks — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:result-validation:next-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 15760,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Validate known passwords and context-specific reuse\n\n**When:** A password tied to a plausible user and service\n\n**Still required:** Correct local/domain/application identity, reachable compatible service, accepted authentication and account state\n\n[[tracks/05 Credentials.canvas|Validate known passwords and context-specific reuse → 05 Credentials]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:result-validation:next-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 16067,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Maintain state and select the next evidence-producing test\n\n**When:** Several hosts, identities, routes or competing hypotheses need coordination\n\n**Still required:** Explicit scope/objective and a record of observations, unknowns and available capabilities\n\n[[tracks/12 Evidence and Reporting.canvas|Maintain state and select the next evidence-producing test → 12 Evidence and Reporting]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:windows-discovery:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 70,
      "y": 16698,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Enumerate reachable endpoints from a Windows source\n\nThe useful vantage point is a Windows host without Nmap",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:windows-discovery:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 570,
      "y": 16658,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 228,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\nGet-NetIPConfiguration\nGet-NetRoute -AddressFamily IPv4\nTest-NetConnection TARGET -Port 445\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:windows-discovery:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 16638,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nThe service is reachable from this Windows source; this can reveal a useful vantage point unavailable from Kali.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:windows-discovery:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 16884,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nConfirm application/authentication and whether a forward or a native client can use that route.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:windows-discovery:checks",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 570,
      "y": 16946,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### Validate the condition\n\n```powershell\nGet-NetIPConfiguration\nGet-NetRoute -AddressFamily IPv4\nTest-NetConnection TARGET -Port PORT\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:windows-discovery:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 16588,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nA protocol request works from this source: choose an authorized service client or suitable tunnel.\n\n**Verify:** Associate each result with the actual Windows source and selected port; do not claim UDP or full-port coverage.\n\n[[notes/discovery.md#windows-discovery|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:windows-discovery:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 16929,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nThe selected service is conclusively closed from this source: choose another observed endpoint.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:windows-discovery:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 17150,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nTcpTestSucceeded False with uncertain routing/firewall does not prove the host is down.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:windows-discovery:action",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 16588,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 228,
      "text": "### Procedure entry — full sequence in the note\n\n```powershell\nTest-NetConnection -ComputerName TARGET -Port PORTS\n```\n\n[[notes/discovery.md#windows-discovery|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:windows-discovery:next-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 16906,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Discover pivot interfaces, routes and internal service context\n\n**When:** A foothold exposes an interface/subnet or a loopback-only service\n\n**Still required:** A usable pivot process/identity and explicit scope; both forward and return directions must be understood\n\n[[tracks/10 Pivoting.canvas|Discover pivot interfaces, routes and internal service context → 10 Pivoting]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:windows-discovery:next-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 17213,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Use WinRM, WinRS or PowerShell remoting\n\n**When:** A WinRM listener and a candidate endpoint-authorized account\n\n**Still required:** Reachable HTTP(S) listener, accepted authentication and endpoint/session configuration permissions; hash/ticket support depends on client/context\n\n[[tracks/09 Active Directory.canvas|Use WinRM, WinRS or PowerShell remoting → 09 Active Directory]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:windows-discovery:next-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 17544,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Validate uncertain results and rebuild the service queue\n\n**When:** Scanners disagree, a result is ambiguous, or a new identity changes accessible behavior\n\n**Still required:** A selected endpoint and a test that can resolve the decision-changing uncertainty\n\n**Validate uncertain results and rebuild the service queue — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:unknown-port:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 70,
      "y": 18175,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Discriminate unknown listeners and use scanner alternatives\n\nA nonstandard listener, slow TCP discovery or a scanner-specific candidate",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:unknown-port:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 570,
      "y": 18135,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 204,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\nnmap -Pn -sV --version-all -p PORT TARGET\nnc -nv TARGET PORT\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:unknown-port:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 18115,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nTLS and an HTTP redirect suggest a hostname-selected web application rather than an attack tied to the port number.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:unknown-port:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 18361,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nReproduce the hostname/TLS request and confirm exact software/configuration.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:unknown-port:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 18065,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nA correctly addressed request produces the application: move to its normal behavior map.\n\n**Verify:** Confirm the endpoint through independent application behavior and preserve the rate/scope used for discovery.\n\n[[notes/discovery.md#unknown-port|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:unknown-port:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 18406,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nThe banner disproves the originally assumed protocol: remove that service hypothesis.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:unknown-port:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 18627,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nNo banner may mean a client-first protocol, TLS or filtering; use a discriminating normal request.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:unknown-port:action",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 18065,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Procedure entry — full sequence in the note\n\n```bash\nrustscan -a TARGET -r 1-65535 --ulimit 5000 -- \\\n  -Pn -sV -sC -oA rustscan-followup\n```\n\n[[notes/discovery.md#unknown-port|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:unknown-port:next-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 18407,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Identify applications and validate selected NSE checks\n\n**When:** A listener has a port-based label or uncertain version\n\n**Still required:** A reachable selected port; scripts must match the application and permitted assessment behavior\n\n**Identify applications and validate selected NSE checks — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:unknown-port:next-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 18714,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Establish scheme, host, redirects and request state\n\n**When:** An HTTP endpoint, redirect or hostname-dependent response\n\n**Still required:** Correct scheme/port and virtual host; saved cookies/headers for authenticated comparisons\n\n[[tracks/03 Web.canvas|Establish scheme, host, redirects and request state → 03 Web]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:unknown-port:next-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 19021,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Match a public exploit to the actual component and configuration\n\n**When:** A product/version clue, advisory or component-specific public PoC\n\n**Still required:** Exact vulnerable build/configuration, required access and endpoint behavior; reviewable source and a verifiable expected effect\n\n[[tracks/04 Public Exploits.canvas|Match a public exploit to the actual component and configuration → 04 Public Exploits]]",
      "color": "5"
